SamenvattingReady for the next step in production? Contribute to quality and efficiency! In this role, you are responsible for disassembling, cleaning, testing, and reassembling returned products. This way, you give electronics a second life and directly contribute to a more sustainable process. Do you enjoy varied work and work with precision? Then this is your opportunity!Over de functieYour responsibilities include:
- disassembling returned modems, routers, and parts;
- cleaning components and devices;
- testing individual components and complete products;
- assembling refurbished devices;
- accurately recording test outcomes.

In this company you work from monday to friday, from 07:30 till 16:30.
Over het bedrijfThis company offers comprehensive logistics services with a strong focus on sustainability. They turn returned electronics into valuable refurbished products using high quality and efficient processes.
Wat wij vragen- Energetic and able to stand for 8 hours;
- Interest in electronics and technical tasks;
- Reasonable English language skills;
- Precise, motivated, and team-oriented.

Wat wij bieden- Hourly wage starting from €15.26
- Holiday allowance and vacation hours accrual
- Travel allowance / reimbursement
- High chance of a permanent contract after 6 months
- Realistic opportunities for personal and professional development
- Monthly drinks / social gatherings
- Working in a close-knit and friendly team

Meer informatieWill you start working as a production worker in Bleiswijk? You can apply within just 2 minutes.
Any questions? Thomas will be happy to help you via +31 6 237 235 54 (also WhatsApp) or by email at t.dupuis@carriere.com.

Are you an avid cleaner or cleaner? Do you want to make sure that vacationing guests can start their vacation with a good feeling? Then read on quickly! 

We are looking for part-time cleaning employees for vacation park de Leistert in Roggel. Mondays and Fridays are the so-called changeover days when new guests arrive at the cottage. On these days it is important that the bungalows and vacation homes are cleaned properly. You do this with a whole team of enthusiastic and motivated cleaners. Together you make sure that everything looks spic and span. 

Tasks you will perform include:

- Making beds;
- Cleaning the kitchen, bathroom, bedroom and living room;
- Dusting and mopping everything; 
- Identifying defects and passing them on to the right people so that they can be repaired in a timely manner.

The work takes place on Mondays and Fridays between 9 a.m. and 3 p.m. Would you like to work more? Please let us know so we can discuss the possibilities! 

- You are a motivated cleaner who knows how to get things done;
- You speak the Dutch, English or German language;
- It is no problem to come to the location in Roggel (public transport is also possible); 
- You are available at least on Mondays and Fridays.

In the vacation periods it is always extra busy, it is important that you are flexible in these periods!

SamenvattingDo you see a challenge in loading, unloading and carefully checking freight? Do you want to work in a dynamic, international environment? Become a Warehouse Mail Employee at Schiphol-Rijk, full-time! Good work!Over de functieAs a Warehouse Post employee, you will play an important role in loading and unloading goods and work closely with your team in a dynamic environment. Flexibility, cooperation and customer orientation are key. What will you do?
- Mail acceptance and processing;
- Sorting mail bags and parcels;
- Performing light administrative tasks;
- ULD assembly and disassembly;
- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Transport on the platform

You will work in a diverse team and follow a schedule with three different shifts:
- Morning shift: 07:00 - 15:30 
- Afternoon shift: 15:00 - 23:30 
- Night shift: 23:00 - 07:00 

Over het bedrijfAt this leading company, you will have the opportunity to work in a dynamic environment where teamwork and efficiency are key. As a leading player in the logistics sector, the organization offers a challenging work environment where you can further develop your skills and play an important role in the efficient handling of shipments.
Wat wij vragen- Have logistics experience;
- Willing to follow internal courses;
- Good Command of the Dutch or/and English language;
- Ready to work physically;
- You can obtain a Certificate of No Objection (VGB) ( which we will apply for) meaning you should have at least 8 years of registration within the EU.

These points are very important to start working as a Warehouse Post Employee at Schiphol-Rijk. We are also curious about who you are. Curious about your talents, background and ideas. Surprise us.
Wat wij bieden- € 16.70  € 16,99 gross salary per hour, depending on relevant work experience (including 2,5% year-end bonus) 
- Supplements for evening, night weekend shifts and public holidays, ranging from 125% to 140%
- Holiday allowances of 200%
- Weekly payments with 8.33% vac
